  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One file, one connection",
      "items": [
        "db.ts opens the SQLite file named by LEDGER_PATH once per process; every other module reaches it through getDb()",
        "index.ts is a barrel: it re-exports every module here and the two Langfuse ones, so callers import from src/ledger/index.js"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Who reads what",
      "items": [
        "MCP gate: elisions (expand_elision, ask_elision), cache-deps, protections, decisions and repo-index (the open-decisions step), memory (read only)",
        "Model gate: distill (one decision per result, resent every turn), memory (write), events",
        "Dashboard and metrics read events; the dashboard also counts the learned protections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The Langfuse copy",
      "items": [
        "writeEvent formats the row (format.ts) and queues it (sink.ts) in the same file; nothing leaves until the flush",
        "Rows rejected repeatedly are parked in langfuse_dead_letter so one bad row never blocks the queue"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
